{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .litehive/tasks/T-0106-add-parallel-worker-fanout-within-a-single-task/task.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: T-0106\nslug: add-parallel-worker-fanout-within-a-single-task\ntitle: Add parallel worker fanout within a single task\ndepends_on:\n- T-0070\ntask_type: null\nengine: null\nmodel: null\nmode: implementation\nstatus: flagged\npipeline_status: implementing\npriority: medium\npm_complexity: complex\nplanned_effort: l\ncreated_at: '2026-04-01T15:05:40+00:00'\nupdated_at: '2026-04-04T03:03:14+00:00'\ngoal: ''\nacceptance_criteria:\n- The `implementing` stage can launch more than one SWE worker for a single task from\n  a deterministic local plan, and the runner does not advance the task to `testing`\n  until all launched workers have reached a terminal state.\n- Litehive persists per-worker runtime state and artifacts while fanout is in progress,\n  including worker identity, role/engine, status, path, and recent progress, so a\n  live run no longer collapses to a single `active_subagent`.\n- Task observability surfaces parallel worker state clearly in status/reporting output,\n  showing multiple active or recently finished workers for the same task instead of\n  only one active/last worker.\n- If a fanout run is interrupted or a worker fails, the task remains recoverable at\n  the same stage with enough persisted worker context to diagnose or resume/retry\n  deterministically; it must not silently leave ambiguous single-worker runtime state.\n- Focused tests cover successful multi-worker fanout for one task, persisted live\n  worker state, status/summary rendering for multiple workers, and interrupted or\n  failed fanout behavior.\nconstraints: []\nplan: []\nhuman_checkpoints: []\nsubagents:\n- id: SA-0001\n  role: planner\n  engine: codex\n  status: completed\n  path: subagents/SA-0001-planner\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0002\n  role: swe\n  engine: codex\n  status: completed\n  path: subagents/SA-0002-swe\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0003\n  role: swe\n  engine: codex\n  status: completed\n  path: subagents/SA-0003-swe\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0004\n  role: qa\n  engine: codex\n  status: completed\n  path: subagents/SA-0004-qa\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0005\n  role: swe\n  engine: codex\n  status: completed\n  path: subagents/SA-0005-swe\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0006\n  role: qa\n  engine: codex\n  status: completed\n  path: subagents/SA-0006-qa\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0007\n  role: swe\n  engine: codex\n  status: interrupted\n  path: subagents/SA-0007-swe\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\n- id: SA-0009\n  role: recovery\n  engine: claude\n  status: failed\n  path: subagents/SA-0009-recovery\n  sandboxed: false\n  sandbox_summary: host\ngit:\n  auto_commit: true\n  commit_message: 'litehive: complete T-0106 add-parallel-worker-fanout-within-a-single-task'\n  commit_sha: null\n  checkpoint_base_sha: null\n  checkpoint_attempts: 0\n  rolled_back_checkpoint_attempt: null\n  worktree_path: .litehive/worktrees/T-0106-add-parallel-worker-fanout-within-a-single-task\nretry_policy:\n  max_retries: null\ncreated_from: null\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
