{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'uv run litehive report --verdict pass --role swe --step implementing --message $'\"'Implemented deterministic parallel SWE fanout for the implementing stage, persisted per-worker runtime state/artifacts, and surfaced multiple active/recent workers in status and snapshot outputs.\\\\n\\\\nVerified acceptance criteria:\\\\n- Implementing fanout now derives deterministic worker slots from the task plan, launches multiple SWE workers in parallel, aggregates their stage reports, and only advances to testing after every launched worker reaches a terminal result.\\\\n- Runtime persistence now keeps per-worker identity and live state in runtime subagent state/session artifacts, including worker_key, assignment, role, engine, status, path, pid, continuation, and recent transcript snippet while workers are still running.\\\\n- Status/observability output now shows multiple active and recent workers for one task instead of collapsing to a single active_subagent/last_subagent view, and web snapshot/session views also honor multiple active workers.\\\\n- Interrupted fanout runs remain recoverable at implementing with completed and interrupted worker records preserved in runtime state/artifacts rather than leaving ambiguous single-worker state.\\\\n\\\\nFocused tests run:\\\\n- uv run pytest -q tests/test_runner_workflow.py -k \\\"fanout or interrupted_fanout\\\"\\\\n- uv run pytest -q tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py -k \\\"multiple_live_worker_states\\\"\\\\n- uv run pytest -q tests/test_observability_and_status.py -k \\\"multiple_active_subagents\\\"\\\\n- uv run pytest -q tests/test_runner_workflow.py tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py tests/test_observability_and_status.py -k \\\"fanout or worker_states or multiple_active_subagents\\\"\\\\n\\\\nSTAGE_RESULT:\\\\n{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Added deterministic parallel SWE fanout with persisted live worker state and multi-worker observability for implementing\\\",\\\"files_changed\\\":[\\\"litehive/cli.py\\\",\\\"litehive/models.py\\\",\\\"litehive/observability.py\\\",\\\"litehive/runtime.py\\\",\\\"litehive/subagents.py\\\",\\\"litehive/tasks.py\\\",\\\"litehive/web.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_observability_and_status.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_runner_workflow.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py\\\"],\\\"tests\\\":{\\\"added\\\":4,\\\"passing\\\":4},\\\"warnings\\\":[\\\"Workspace also has unrelated changes in .litehive/tasks/T-0077-add-structured-pm-task-edit-actions-during-grooming/thread.yaml\\\"],\\\"follow_up_tasks\\\":[],\\\"acceptance_criteria\\\":[\\\"The implementing stage can launch more than one SWE worker for a single task from a deterministic local plan, and the runner does not advance the task to testing until all launched workers have reached a terminal state.\\\",\\\"Litehive persists per-worker runtime state and artifacts while fanout is in progress, including worker identity, role/engine, status, path, and recent progress, so a live run no longer collapses to a single active_subagent.\\\",\\\"Task observability surfaces parallel worker state clearly in status/reporting output, showing multiple active or recently finished workers for the same task instead of only one active/last worker.\\\",\\\"If a fanout run is interrupted or a worker fails, the task remains recoverable at the same stage with enough persisted worker context to diagnose or resume/retry deterministically; it must not silently leave ambiguous single-worker runtime state.\\\",\\\"Focused tests cover successful multi-worker fanout for one task, persisted live worker state, status/summary rendering for multiple workers, and interrupted or failed fanout behavior.\\\"]}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
